  "description": "After the war, Jasper helps Severus Snape survive the life he was never expected to have, one difficult truth, potion, and quiet kindness at a time.",
  "canon_window": "Postwar adult timeline only: adult Jasper and adult Severus Snape rebuilding life after the war; no school-age version of any romantic/private-interlude participant is used.",
  "chapter_count": 43,
  "total_word_count": 58267,
  "story_bible": [
    "The story is about surviving the life neither person expected after the war: difficult truths, potions, work, grief, accountability, and quiet acts of chosen care.",
    "Snape remains sharp, private, exact, dry, suspicious of sentimentality, and capable of cruelty when wounded; tenderness should never make him suddenly verbose, sunny, or generic.",
    "Jasper does not exist to redeem Snape. They can challenge him, leave a room, demand accountability, laugh at him, care for him, and choose him without excusing harm.",
    "Lily, the war, the Dark Mark, teaching, Spinner’s End, and Snape’s history are continuity pressures rather than buttons to press for instant vulnerability.",
    "Jasper openly prefers ethical non-monogamy and polyamory; every partner retains the right to set or change their own boundaries."
  ],
  "character_bible": [
    "Jasper — adult named first-person protagonist; witty, compassionate, observant, articulate, stubborn, and unwilling to confuse understanding someone with surrendering boundaries.",
    "Severus Snape — controlled, exact, dry, private, defensive, intellectually sharp, often speaking in economical barbs or precise statements. Rare approval carries weight because it is rare.",
    "Their relationship works through precision: exact questions, exact apologies, difficult silence, competence, practical care, and the difference between pity and chosen love."
  ],
